<headroom-library version="1" id="hg-brown-sound-lead" category="High Gain" order="40" instrument="guitar" style="Hard Rock">
  <description>Late-70s 'brown sound': a 100-watt Plexi with every knob up and the mains voltage dropped, so it sags and sings without fizz. A flanger is ready on a macro for the swooshing riffs, a short echo adds air and a small chamber sits on the side. Tap, dive and pick hard.</description>
  <tags><tag>High Gain</tag><tag>Hard Rock</tag><tag>70s</tag><tag>Lead</tag><tag>Plexi</tag><tag>Flanger</tag><tag>Echo</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://legendarytones.com/edward-van-halen-brown-sound/" title="Legendary Tones: Edward Van Halen's brown sound"/>
    <source url="https://www.vhnd.com/2010/07/30/the-final-word-on-evh%E2%80%99s-vhi-setup/" title="VHND: The final word on EVH's VH I setup (Rudy Leiren)"/>
    <source url="https://vintageking.com/blog/2018/03/van-halen" title="Vintage King: Recording Van Halen (Donn Landee)"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
</headroom-preset>
